# Mortgage

// the whole loan on one page. The headline at the top cites the
// derivation at the bottom - forward references resolve, so the
// reading order is yours to choose: summary first, algebra after.

## The headline
// monthly payment
&25
// everything you pay
&26
// what the bank keeps
&27
// the last payment lands
&28

## The loan
principal = 420000
rate = 5.8% / 12
months = 360

## The derivation
// standard amortization: P * r / (1 - (1 + r)^-months)
factor = (1 + rate) ^ months
payment = principal * rate / (1 - factor ^ -1)
paid = payment * months
interest = paid - principal
payoff = today + 30 years
